+# Daily Grind browser tools
+
+The homepage registers client-side WebMCP tools when
+`document.modelContext.registerTool` is available in a secure browser context.
+Browsers without that API retain the normal page and order controls.
+
+| Tool | Input | Effect |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `query_seasonal_menu` | `{ "query": "oat" }` (query optional) | Returns matching displayed drink names, descriptions, and IDs without changing the page. |
+| `order_drink` | `{ "drinkId": "maple-oat-latte", "quantity": 2 }` | Adds drinks to the visible local order. Quantity defaults to 1 and must be an integer from 1 to 10 per invocation. |
+| `highlight_drink` | `{ "drinkId": "cold-brew" }` | Highlights, scrolls to, and focuses the requested drink card. |
+
+Drink IDs are `maple-oat-latte`, `dark-roast-espresso`, and `cold-brew`.
+Invalid inputs return structured errors without changing the order or highlight.
+Orders exist only in the current page's memory, reset on reload, and never charge
+money or send an order to a café. The page buttons use the same ordering action
+as the tools. The menu is read from the displayed cards rather than a separate
+catalog. Registrations use abort signals for page lifecycle cleanup and are
+restored on return from the browser's back/forward cache.
+
+Run the non-browser checks with:
+
+```sh
+node --test menu-tools.test.mjs
+node --check daily-grind.mjs
+```
